## 3. Configuration: From Difference to Information

Once distinction exists — once there are at least two possible states — information becomes definable. In its minimal formal sense, information is the answer to "which of the possible states is actual?" The measure of this selective capacity is Shannon entropy: for a set of possible states with probabilities $p_i$,

$$H = -\sum_i p_i \log_2 p_i.$$

But information is not merely an abstract measure; it has physical consequences. Landauer's principle states that any logically irreversible erasure of one bit of information must dissipate at least $k_B T \ln 2$ of energy into the environment [2]. This directly ties information processing to thermodynamics, and demonstrates that information is not a passive descriptor of physics but a participant in physical law.

Wheeler's "It from Bit" programme elevates this to an ontological claim: every physical entity derives its existence from bits of information. A stronger, empirically grounded version today is "It from Qubit," where quantum entanglement is the fundamental substrate. The discovery that black hole entropy is proportional to horizon area, $S_{\text{BH}} = k_B A / 4 l_P^2$, led to the holographic principle. Within the framework of the AdS/CFT correspondence, the Ryu–Takayanagi formula makes this precise [3]:

$$S_A = \frac{\text{Area}(\gamma_A)}{4G_N},$$

where $S_A$ is the entanglement entropy of a boundary subregion and $\gamma_A$ is the minimal bulk surface. This equation shows that, in AdS, spacetime geometry is directly constructed from quantum entanglement.

**The de Sitter problem: new developments.** The original version of this paper correctly flagged the gap between AdS holography and the de Sitter universe we actually inhabit. Significant progress has now been made on precisely this front. Considering two antipodal observers in de Sitter space, researchers have illustrated how spacetime connectivity between the holographic screens located on the stretched horizons emerges from holographic entanglement [arxiv](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.14889) , through a covariant holographic entanglement entropy prescription including quantum corrections [25]. Furthermore, Dong, Silverstein, and Torroba have proposed a new example of entanglement knitting spacetime together, where the conjectured dual of de Sitter in $d+1$ dimensions involves two coupled CFT sectors constrained by residual $d$-dimensional gravity [arxiv](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1804.08623) [31]. Imposing strong subadditivity and related inequalities provides powerful constraints on any entropy functional built from de Sitter Green's functions [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/html/2508.14478) , and recent work is actively constructing a self-consistent holographic entanglement entropy prescription valid in de Sitter space [32].

These developments substantially strengthen the claim that geometry emerges from entanglement across cosmological settings. While a complete and experimentally confirmed holographic dual for our de Sitter universe remains an open research programme, the analogy is no longer merely motivating — it is increasingly buttressed by concrete proposals.

We therefore affirm that **Configuration** is fundamental, and its quantum measure is entanglement; spacetime geometry appears as an emergent manifestation of entanglement in appropriate limits.

